          "lore_md": "Fictional-registry entry (plausible canon-adjacent). The clan's most expensive exhibit and its best-kept heresy: something serpentine, ancient, and — theologically impossible — hibernating inside a corporate vault in Dubai. The inner temples call it a relic of the God-Killer; the Seneschals call it an asset with appreciating yield, because the thing dreams, and whoever holds the dream holds leverage over every congregation that shares bloodline to it. Access requires three Faithful, one Seneschal, and a contract written in a language the museum world pretends is Etruscan. SchreckNET flagged the vault's power draw in 2019: it triples once a year, on the same three nights as the Alexandria festival. Analysts advise against the obvious conclusion. Analysts take it anyway.",
