      "lore_md": "The Ravnos are wanderers, illusionists and thieves, and their name on SchreckNET is a warning label, not a courtesy. Their founder Zapathasura rose during the Week of Nightmares in 1999 and was burned out of the sky over Bangladesh by three Kuei-jin bodhisattvas, a nuclear dawn and whatever else the Jyhad could aim at him. The clan that survived him has been orphaned twice over: once by the pogroms that followed his waking, once by the Second Inquisition, which finds their signature easy to flag because it always appears where nothing is real.\n\nThey have no princes and no courts worth the name. They keep to caravans, circus lots, river banks and festival seasons; a Ravnos warren is wherever the tents are tonight. Their discipline of Chimerstry turns air into evidence — illusory coins, illusory doors, illusory witnesses — and their reputation for fraud makes them useful to every sect and trusted by none of it.\n\nRegistry note: the clan will not confirm its own numbers. Death-listings below carry the Week of Nightmares uncertainty banner where applicable. The vizier-lineages (Phuri Dae) insist the founder’s death was itself an illusion. SchreckNET neither confirms nor denies.",
