          "lore_md": "London fell to the Second Inquisition, but Osric kept his seats — the opera house never checks the box holder, only the tuxedo. He survived by becoming the most boring kind of famous: a name on a plaque. Osric's reviews of elder \"performances\" have started fights and ended careers. SchreckNET credits him with warning three princes about SI raids via single-word reviews.",
          "photo": "assets/img/char_toreador15.png"
