          "lore_md": "Files bone-script notes into wall niches among the mummified brothers. WALL-CLERK: notes placed at dusk are found moved one corridor deeper by dawn, still legible. He treats this as postal service and pays it in rosaries. Directive: send nothing you would not want read aloud. Two summons letters sent via wall never arrived; the senders stopped writing first.",
          "photo": "assets/img/char_harbingers27.png"
