      "weakness": "Permanent animal features accumulate with every frenzy, and the pack harness of the Vaulderie chafes against their solitary instincts.",
      "lore_md": "The Sabbat Gangrel serve as scouts, trackers and hunters, split into two branches that despise each other politely. The Country Gangrel keep the old ways: Animalism, Fortitude, Protean, long nights at the edge of the wild where the city light dies. The City Gangrel traded Fortitude for Celerity and Obfuscate and hunt inside the infrastructure itself, storm drains, rail spurs, heating grids.\n\nBoth branches feed the war machine. A crusade moves at the speed of its scouts, and the antitribu scouts are the best in the sect. They are also the most likely to walk away, which is why every pack watches its Gangrel closer than its Brujah.\n\nSchreckNET reads them through the animals and the infrastructure. Rat convoys, silent livestock, thermal dips in steam lines, gate latency, chalk arrows. The registry has never intercepted a radio call from an antitribu Gangrel. They do not use radios. They use the world.\n\nStanding directive: antitribu Gangrel files inherit the animal-warning protocols of mainline Gangrel files. If a city goes quiet for a night, file it under both clans and wait.",
