      "weakness": "Funeral duties come first: every agent must conduct or oversee the rites owed to the dead of their host pack, and the dead collect before the living do. Their necromancy is housebreaking for the underworld.",
      "lore_md": "The Family loaned its antitribu to the sword the way a bank loans money it expects to lose: begrudgingly, at interest, with collateral. Hecata antitribu serve Sabbat packs as undertakers, notaries of the dead, and auditors of Final Deaths. They are tolerated because no pack can argue with a census of its own corpses.\n\nTheir weakness is procedural: the rites of the dead come before the orders of the living. A pack that tries to skip a funeral on its books loses the antitribu services at the worst hour, and the dead, per registry observation, do not stay patient.\n\nStanding directive: never purchase a burial, a plot, or a blessing; log every name the agents display, flag any date of death that precedes its funeral by more than a season, and file under GOODS-AHEAD. The Family sells the future and calls it inventory.",
