      "weakness": "They feed on rejection: the clan taste turned inside out, craving blood only from those who despise them, and building empires out of debts other Kindred would rather forget.",
      "lore_md": "SchreckNET assessment: Ventrue antitribu are the aristocracy of the lost ledger. Where the clan proper buys loyalty, the sword-branch buys obligation — debts, bonds, contracts, mortgages on havens and on names. They operate inside Camarilla cities as creditors, auditors, and proxy brokers, and their weapon is paperwork no prince can burn because it is legally true.\n\nThe registry separates them from the clan by behavior, not by look: a Ventrue who never collects in vitae, always in obligation, is antitribu until proven otherwise. Their feeding restriction makes them patient; humiliation is their vintage.\n\nThey have financed Sabbat sieges and bought Camarilla investigations with the same portfolio, and at least two of the nine debts on this dossier cross both sects at once, which is why the file is classified nodes-only.\n\nStanding directive: sign nothing, co-sign nothing, guarantee nothing. Log every offer with the exact wording. If a contract cites a debt you do not remember owing, it is real, and it is already old.",
